\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. All things which live below the sky,
\par Or move within the sea,
\par Are the creatures of the Lord most high,
\par And brothers unto me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. I love to hear the robin sing,
\par Perched on the highest bough;
\par To see the rook with purple wing
\par Follow the shining plough.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. I love to watch the swallow skim
\par The river in his flight;
\par To mark, when day is growing dim,
\par The glow-worm's silvery light;
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. The sea-gull whiter than the foam,
\par The fish that dart beneath;
\par The lowing cattle coming home;
\par The goats upon the heath.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Beneath His heaven there's a room for all;
\par He gives to all their meat;
\par He sees the meanest sparrow fall
\par Unnoticed in the street.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Almighty Father, King of kings,
\par The Lover of the meek,
\par Make me a friend of helpless things,
\par Defender of the weak.
\par Amen.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

